# .env.production holds only the Contact Worker URL - public, and the build
# needs it - so it is the one env file that is tracked.
!.env.production
!.env.example

# Raw drop-off files at the repo root: source screenshots before redaction
# (some still show real client names and the Half Brain Solutions branding)
# and raw testimonial video exports (one is 194MB, over GitHub's own limit).
# The processed, redacted, web-sized versions actually used by the site
# live under public/ and are tracked normally - the single `*` below only
# matches root-level files, never anything inside a subfolder like public/.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.mov
